    "abstract": "The southern Iraq\u2019s wetlands face many challenges that affect their environment and the livelihoods of local communities, including the problem of drought. This study aims to evaluate both meteorological and agricultural drought conditions within the marshland regions over a four-decade span (1984, 1994, 2004, 2014, and 2024). Satellite imagery from the Landsat multispectral scanner (MSS), Thematic mapper (TM), Enhanced thematic mapper (ETM) was employed to derive the vegetation condition index (VCI) to assess agricultural drought and climatic data were used to derive reconnaissance drought index (RDI) to assess meteorological drought. The result showed that the severity of the meteorological droughts increased over the period. In 1984, most of areas were under no drought condition while in 2024, most of the areas were under moderate to severe drought condition. The study also revealed that there was mild meteorological drought in 1994, but the agricultural drought conditions was severe and extreme. Overall, it suggests that the climate change and water scarcity have exacerbated agricultural drought condition in the region.",
    "field": "Drought assessment",
    "problem": "Southern Iraq's wetlands face escalating environmental degradation and drought, but assessing the long-term severity is complicated by the combined impacts of climate change, water scarcity, and human interventions such as dam construction and extensive drainage projects.",
    "method": "This study assesses agricultural and meteorological drought in Southern Iraq's wetlands by deriving the Vegetation Condition Index (VCI) from satellite imagery and the Reconnaissance Drought Index (RDI) from climatic data to analyze conditions over a four-decade span.",
    "task": "The task is to assess agricultural and meteorological drought in Southern Iraq's wetlands from 1984 to 2024 by using the Vegetation Condition Index (VCI) and Reconnaissance Drought Index (RDI) derived from satellite imagery and climatic data.",
